  "raw": {
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/830": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Student Engagement",
      "description": "Category: Student Affairs - Support Personnel JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Are you ready to coordinate programming that doesn’t just fill a calendar, but builds belonging? Join Flagler College as the Coordinator of Student Engagement to help shape a connected and inclusive campus community in historic Saint Augustine. The Coordinator of Student Engagement assists in the overall coordination and supervision of the student activities program including, but not limited to, weekly evening events, leadership development series, field trips, campus-wide collaborative programming and events demonstrating a commitment to the Core Values of Flagler College. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree in a related field An understanding of and commitment to student belonging Ability to understand the needs of students Ability to collaborate and build relationships with students, faculty, and staff Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong management and organizational skills 1-2 years’ experience in student activities, leadership development and/or campus programming. Student affairs experience with an emphasis on student development strongly preferred 1 or more years of advising students on personal and academic matters CHARACTERISTICS PREFERRED Ability to adjust quickly to changing needs on a daily basis. Ability to apply strong problem solving and conflict resolution skills Maintain productive and effective, inclusive working relationships amongst diverse populations including staff, faculty, administration, students, and other internal and external constituents PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Ability to manage multiple projects and competing priorities simultaneously Ability to train and evaluate performance, taking corrective action as needed WORKING CONDITIONS AND PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Sedentary work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involved sitting most of the time and occasionally walking and standing. Climbing, walking, crouching, repetitive motions, and ability to communicate appropriately with students/colleagues. Occasional hours outside the normal College workday to attend events, specifically nights and weekends. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Supports programming efforts through the following: Leadership development program Inclusive programming Collaborative programming with other Student Affairs offices including health and wellness, housing operations and residential living, campus recreation and career development Family Weekend On and off campus programming and field trips Coordinates and/or provides support for night-time programming to include: Night programming series Movie Showings Guest Speakers Collaborative programming with campus partners Student events and student-sponsored events Serves as point of contact for student workers Manages social media and marketing for department. Reviews and tracks all expenditures as they relate to student activities budget. Maintains accurate records of student involvement in co-curricular programming events, databases and files, track data and expenditures, schedules building and facilities, compiles information for reports, processes emails and creates posters and fliers as needed. Provides administrative support to student clubs and organizations as needed Assumes other duties as assigned Serve on campus-wide committees as needed."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/833": {
      "title": "Lab Manager",
      "description": "Category: Academic Affairs - Staff JobSchedule: Part time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Are you an organized, adaptable lab professional ready for a meaningful role in a fast-paced academic setting? Flagler College’s Natural Sciences Department is seeking an Interim Natural Sciences Lab Manager to support lab facilities, inventory, equipment, and safety protocols. The Natural Sciences Department at Flagler College is seeking applicants for an interim Chemistry and Physics Lab Manager. Partnering with the Natural Sciences Lab Manager, the interim lab manager will support teaching and research labs by overseeing laboratory facilities, inventory, equipment, safety protocols, and regulatory compliance. This position requires a versatile technical background spanning chemistry, physics, and science education, alongside superior organizational skills and flexibility within a dynamic, fast-paced academic environment. Bachelor’s degree in Chemistry or a related field required. Strong scientific technical background including reagent preparation, glassware handling, procedure execution, and equipment troubleshooting. Extensive experience interpreting safety data sheets, disposing of chemical waste, and using personal protective equipment. Exceptional organizational, time-management, and prioritization skills, with the ability to delegate tasks effectively. Consistent attention to detail and the ability to work independently or collaboratively. Excellent verbal and written communication skills between a diverse range of management, faculty, students, staff, and vendors. Physical ability to lift/carry up to 30 pounds, bend, stoop, reach, and safely operate equipment and business machinery. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Support teaching lab activities by preparing reagents, equipment, and supplies. Uphold comprehensive safety protocols for users of all experience levels; foster a proactive culture of laboratory safety and compliance. Facilitate storage and disposal of hazardous materials in accordance with safety procedures and local, state, and federal regulations. Assist with the management, supervision, and training of work-study students. Perform and oversee the repair and maintenance of scientific equipment, instrumentation, and computers across teaching, research, and preparation labs. Coordinate with the Natural Sciences Lab Manager and Department Chair to purchase supplies and maintain inventory. Work with the Natural Sciences Lab Manager, Maintenance, and Housekeeping to keep the laboratory facilities and equipment clean and safe. Coordinate with the Natural Sciences Lab Manager and Environmental Health and Safety department to maintain a safe environment within regulatory compliance. Drive College vehicles and carts. Additional duties as needed"
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/827": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Category: Enrollment Management - Financial Aid JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States The Financial Aid Counselor advises students and parents on all matters pertaining to the financial aid program and assists with the administration of financial aid awarding. The Financial Aid Counselor advises students and parents on all matters pertaining to the financial aid program and assists with the administration of financial aid awarding. Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent required (An acceptable equivalent is an AA degree plus a minimum of 2 years of professional office experience.) Preferred Knowledge and Skills: Effective and professional communication skills both verbally and in writing Possess patience and empathy for students and parents by remaining congenial and respectful under stressful conditions while treating others with dignity and respect Student-focused and collaborative, a cooperative attitude Responsive an accessible by responding promptly with appropriate follow through Analytical skills for the review of documents and student files Computer skills and experience in data entry Proficiency in mathematics Organizational skills and accurate record keeping/data entry Ability to multi-task and work in an environment with frequent interruptions Prior financial aid experience Counsels assigned students and their parents on financial aid matters, including application for federal, state, and institutional aid; application for scholarships, and application for loans. Evaluates students’ financial aid documents for completeness and accuracy, ensuring that federal, state, and institutional eligibility and application requirements are met. Determines financial aid awards, including federal, state, and institutional financial aid awards in compliance with federal, state, and institutional policy, regulation, and law. Performs regular review of incomplete files and corresponds with students and families regarding the forms and information required to complete the students file. Corresponds with students and families regarding the financial aid Award Letter, award acceptance, renewal requirements, and application completion Coordinates closely with the Business Office regarding student aid, student balances, and payment issues. Performs evaluation of student eligibility in accordance with financial aid renewal requirements, and works in conjunction with the Registrar’s Office to review eligibility issues pertaining to grades and hours. Participates in College events to provide information on financial aid matters to the local community including students, prospective students, parents, high school personnel, and other organizations Organizes documents and maintains student financial aid records via both physical file and via enterprise software. Perform duties \\ tasks as prescribed by the Director and Associate Director of Financial Aid"
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/697": {
      "title": "Custodian/Housekeeper",
      "description": "Category: Business Services - Facilities and Maintenance JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Looking for steady, full-time work with great benefits? We’re hiring Custodian/Housekeepers to support our campus community. Enjoy health insurance after 30 days, strong PTO accrual, paid holidays, tuition benefits, and training provided. The Custodian / Housekeeper plays an essential role in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming campus environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. This position supports daily campus operations through routine cleaning, basic upkeep, and facility support tasks. The ideal candidate takes pride in their work, values teamwork, and understands the importance of their contribution to the College community. Training and uniforms are provided. Prior custodial experience is helpful but not required. We value our employees and offer a competitive benefits package, including: Health insurance beginning the first of the month following 30 days of employment Generous paid time off with strong accrual rates Paid holidays Tuition benefits Stable, full-time employment in a supportive campus community MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Ability to understand and follow oral and written instructions in English Ability to communicate effectively in English Basic computer skills Valid state driver’s license and ability to operate a College vehicle Reliable attendance and satisfactory work record Strong interpersonal skills and service-oriented mindset WORKING CONDITIONS AND PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: The physical demands described below are representative of those required to successfully perform the essential functions of this position. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. Ability to stand and walk for extended periods of time Frequent bending, stooping, kneeling, crouching, and reaching Ability to climb stairs and ladders Ability to work overhead and in confined or mechanical spaces Ability to lift, carry, push, and pull up to 50 pounds on a regular basis Ability to operate cleaning equipment and tools, including vacuums, floor buffers, and hand tools Ability to work indoors and outdoors in varying temperatures and weather conditions Manual dexterity sufficient to operate cleaning equipment and computer systems Ability to visually inspect areas to ensure cleanliness and safety Clean and maintain campus buildings including classrooms, offices, restrooms, hallways, stairwells, and common areas Vacuum, sweep, mop, dust, scrub, wax, and polish floors and surfaces Clean interior and exterior glass surfaces including windows, mirrors, and partitions Empty trash and recycling, replace liners, and collect refuse from building interiors and exterior walkways Replenish restroom supplies including paper products and soap Straighten desks and furnishings to return rooms to proper working order Launder and replace linens in guest housing as needed Monitor cleaning supplies and notify supervisor when inventory is low Ensure custodial equipment is maintained and functioning properly Assist with deep cleaning and room preparation during summer and peak periods Report facility repair needs to management Assists with the setup, rearrangement, and breakdown of furniture and equipment for special campus events Perform additional custodial, maintenance, or groundskeeping tasks as assigned"
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/781": {
      "title": "Assistant Athletic Trainer",
      "description": "Category: Athletics - Support Personnel JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Join Flagler College Athletics as an Assistant Athletic Trainer and help protect the health and well-being of student-athletes. This hands-on position provides injury prevention, evaluation, emergency care, treatment, rehabilitation, education, and coverage for assigned practices and competitions. The Assistant Athletic Trainer supports the health and well-being of Flagler College student-athletes through injury prevention, evaluation, management, and rehabilitation. This position combines direct support of student-athletes with operational responsibilities that contribute to the effective delivery of athletic training services. The successful candidate will demonstrate professionalism, teamwork, accountability, sportsmanship, integrity, and a commitment to the missions of Flagler College and the Department of Athletics. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s Degree. NATA Certification or equivalent. CHARACTERISTICS PREFERRED Strong organizational ability. Demonstrated ability to communicate professionally and effectively. Strong work ethic. Positive, enthusiastic approach to job responsibilities. Demonstrated ability to work within a team, placing departmental and institutional priorities and student-athlete well-being above personal advancement. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree. Two years’ experience in the collegiate athletics department. WORKING CONDITIONS AND PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Light work: exerting up to 15 pounds of force occasionally, and/or a negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. Exerting up to 10 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Frequent lifting and carrying, pushing, or pulling objects weighing 10 pounds or more; and/or continuous lifting, carrying, pushing, or pulling 5-10 pounds. Climbing, balancing, reaching, standing, walking, lifting, repetitive motions, and ability to communicate appropriately with students/colleagues. Working early mornings, evenings, and weekends is required. Evaluate acute and chronic injuries. Provide daily treatment which may include emergency care, scheduling appointments, and referrals. Implement prevention and rehabilitation programs for athletes. Assist in maintaining detailed and current medical records. Attend all assigned team competitions and practices. Assist in directing the daily maintenance of athletic training facilities and equipment. Educate athletes on injury prevention, management and return to play. Assist in processing medical insurance claims and related information. Assist in the creation of emergency action plans and policies. Assist in inventory and purchasing of medical supplies. Serve as an approved clinical instructor and mentor undergraduate athletic training students. Assist in administering preseason concussion baseline testing. Assist in organizing weekly doctor’s clinics and random drug testing procedures. Assist with the pre-participation screening and physicals. Adheres to the core covenants of Flagler College Athletics, which are: Professionalism, Teamwork, Accountability, Sportsmanship, and Integrity. Adhere to the mission statements of Flagler College and the Department of Athletics. Perform other related duties as assigned."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/743": {
      "title": "Maintenance Worker-Night Shift",
      "description": "Category: Business Services - Facilities and Maintenance JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Support the daily maintenance and operation of Flagler College’s campus facilities during evening and overnight hours through hands-on repair, maintenance, and operational support. This role helps ensure campus spaces remain safe, functional, and well maintained for students, faculty, staff, and visitors. The Maintenance Technician performs a wide range of general maintenance duties across campus facilities and grounds. Responsibilities include responding to maintenance needs, assisting with repairs, supporting after-hours operational needs, and collaborating with Facilities and Security staff to maintain a safe and efficient campus environment. This position requires flexibility, teamwork, and the ability to perform physically demanding work in a variety of conditions. The evening shift is 1:00pm to 10:00 pm. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Ability to comprehend oral and written instructions Willingness to wear personal protective equipment as needed and to practice safety precautions appropriately Satisfactory work record and attendance Valid State driver’s license and the ability to operate college vehicles CHARACTERISTICS PREFERRED: People skills PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: High school diploma Prior experience or aptitude for mechanical work acquired from on-the-job training or vocational school Basic computer skills WORKING CONDITIONS AND PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Very heavy work: exerting in excess of 100 pounds of force occasionally, and/or an excess of 50 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Climbing, balancing, stooping, kneeling, crouching crawling, reaching, standing, walking, pushing, pulling, lifting, fingering, grasping, and repetitive motions. Receives written and oral work assignments from Maintenance Supervisor and obtains necessary tools and supplies from the maintenance shop. Works extensively with Security to triage and coordinate repairs after normal business hours as they are reported. Performs minor repairs to building fixtures such as minor plumbing and electrical repairs, light bulb changes and light carpentry as required. Performs HVAC air filters changes, lubrication and belt changes as directed by Supervisor. Cleans up work area when done. Notifies Director/Assistant Superintendent of repair supplies and materials needs. Move furniture, or other college-related property as needed. Performs other maintenance, custodial and grounds functions as assigned. May be designated to specialize in such functions as Pool Operator responsible for maintaining chemical levels and checking automatic settings. May assist tradespersons where assistance is needed. Performs other college-related duties as required by the Maintenance Lead, Maintenance Supervisor, Assistant Director of Facilities, and the Executive Director of Facilities."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/838": {
      "title": "Academic Affairs Events and Scheduling Coordinator",
      "description": "Category: Academic Affairs - Staff JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Do you thrive on organization, creativity, and collaboration? Join our Academic Affairs team as the Events and Scheduling Coordinator, where you’ll play a key role in bringing the College’s academic mission to life through purposeful events and seamless scheduling. From coordinating faculty and Academic Affairs led events to managing the details that make each event run smoothly, this position connects people, spaces, and ideas across campus. The Academic Affairs Events and Scheduling Coordinator schedules, promotes, plans, and executes internal and college-sponsored external programs and activities for Academic Affairs (excluding donor and President related events, and Kenan Endowed Professorship), including the implementation and coordination with staff and faculty events and managing internal communication requests for College facilities. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS High school degree required One year related field experience Proficiency with computers, including Microsoft Office Suite CHARACTERISTICS PREFERRED Ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing Ability to work without close supervision and make proper independent decisions Detail and multi-task oriented Ability to maintain confidentiality and to exhibit good judgment in making decisions concurrent with College policy. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Two years related field experience WORKING CONDITIONS AND PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Light work: exerting up to 15 pounds of force occasionally, and/or a negligible mount of force constantly to move objects. Climbing, balancing, reaching, standing, walking, lifting, repetitive motions, and ability to communicate appropriately with students/colleagues; ability to access multi-storied buildings and multiple-level staircases. Must qualify for a Florida driver’s license and the ability to drive a car. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Process all academic scheduling for faculty and Academic Affairs staff events and requested meetings through Saints Connect. This includes confirming space availability and event appropriateness based on the requested event, College’s mission as well as coordinating with other departments on campus for space and required approvals. Event consultation with faculty and Academic Affairs staff on how to implement successful events on campus. Assist in cost estimates, floor plans, and logistics of the event. Coordinate all catering, maintenance, security, and housekeeping needs related to events. Coordinate with Marketing any promotional materials, advertising, social media notifications needs related to events. Foster collaboration between offices to ensure well organized and executed events by meeting with Special Events to ensure all parties have the needed information. Assist in planning and implementation of special events, e.g., Interact regularly with staff, faculty, and Academic Affairs leaders. On-site coordination for internal events and Academic Affairs hosted events that may include evenings and weekends. Schedule and supervise all student work grants. Performs other duties as assigned by Academic Affairs."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/839": {
      "title": "Registrar Clerk",
      "description": "Category: Academic Affairs - Staff JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Do you enjoy helping students succeed from their first class to graduation day? Join us as a Registrar Clerk and be a welcoming face and helpful presence for every student, family, and faculty member who walks through our door. The Registrar Clerk provides frontline service and administrative support to the Registrar’s Office, ensuring the accuracy of student records and the smooth operation of office functions. This position shares responsibility for responding to student, faculty, staff, and parent inquiries; processing student record transactions; and supporting registration and graduation services. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Associate’s degree or equivalent combination of education and related work experience. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel). Strong organizational and customer service skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s degree. Two or more years of customer service experience in higher education or a related field. Knowledge of higher education procedures, student records, and registrar functions. WORK CONDITIONS: Standard office hours (8:00 a.m. – 5:00 p.m.), with occasional evening and weekend hours required (e.g., term registration, graduation ceremony). Work performed under limited direct supervision, requiring discretion, accuracy, and confidentiality. This is a fast-paced environment with frequent interruptions, and the incumbent will be expected to perform with a high degree of accuracy and attention to detail. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Frontline Service & Communication Serves as the first point of contact (in person, phone, email) for the Registrar’s Office with professionalism and a student-centered approach. Responds to inquiries regarding registration, academic records, and general Registrar services. Prepares and distributes enrollment verification letters. Student Records Processing Processes forms and transactions such as name and address updates, transcript requests, enrollment verifications, FERPA releases, course registrations, course withdrawals, paid cancels, and grade changes. Systems & Technology Utilizes multiple software solutions to manage and execute job functions. Assigns, tracks, and resolves service tickets accurately and timely. Office & Event Support Participates in registration periods for all terms (fall, spring, summer, FlagSHIP). Supports office events and initiatives as assigned. Assists the College Registrar in monitoring FERPA compliance and safeguarding the confidentiality of student records."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/840": {
      "title": "Accommodations Exam Clerk",
      "description": "Category: Academic Affairs - Staff JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Are you someone who wants students to feel prepared, supported, and ready to succeed? Flagler College's Disability Resource Center is seeking an Accommodations Exam Clerk to administer exam accommodations with care and confidentiality. The Exam Clerk is a 10-month, full-time, and non-exempt position responsible for coordinating and administering exam accommodations for students registered with the Disability Resource Center (DRC). This role ensures the secure, confidential, and efficient execution of exam-related processes, from scheduling to return, while maintaining compliance with college policies and disability regulations. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High school diploma or equivalent. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Proficiency in Microsoft Office and general office equipment. Strong organizational and time management skills with the ability to handle multiple tasks. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to maintain confidentiality, use sound judgement, and interact effectively with students. WORKING CONDITIONS: Sedentary work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull, or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time and occasionally walking and standing. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Exam Accommodations Coordination Maintain and regularly update the exam accommodations tracking spreadsheet (Excel). Schedule exams for students receiving accommodations in accordance with approved disability services. Arrange and implement intra-exam accommodations such as extended time, reader services, or distraction-reduced environments. Secure and return exams to faculty, ensuring proper handling and confidentiality. Maintain an inventory of all exam-related supplies (e.g., scantrons, exam books, pencils, noise-canceling materials). Proctoring and Monitoring Actively observe students during exams, both in-person and via internal camera systems. Ensure no unauthorized materials or devices are used during the exam. Intervene and document incidents of suspected academic dishonesty, submitting formal reports and notifying faculty and DRC leadership. Exam Request Processing Monitor and manage incoming exam requests via Qualtrics surveys, including requests from both DRC and non-DRC students. Export survey data to spreadsheets and initiate exam scheduling communications. Confirm exam details with both faculty and students, addressing any feedback or discrepancies promptly. Create and send exam request emails using standardized documentation templates. Exam Return Process Determine the appropriate return method (faculty pickup, scanning and emailing, or both). Verify exam completeness and securely scan, name, and save files as needed. Store exams in the designated secure location for faculty retrieval. Complete weekly tracking and reporting of exam return data via Qualtrics and Excel."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/841": {
      "title": "Director of Student Engagement",
      "description": "Category: Student Affairs - Support Personnel JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States Do you know how to turn a campus of students into a community? Join Flagler College as Director of Student Engagement to oversee student activities and organizations and foster a sense of belonging among our students. The Director of Student Engagement is responsible for the coordination and supervision of the student activities program. This encompasses all student clubs and organizations approved by the College. Additionally, the Director oversees activities sponsored by the Multicultural Center and Student Engagement to include weekly evening events, leadership development series, Family Weekend, Alternative Spring Break and events demonstrating a commitment to the Core Values of Flagler College. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master's degree in a related field Ability to understand the needs of students from diverse backgrounds Ability to collaborate and build relationships with students, faculty, and staff Excellent written and verbal communication skills Strong management and organizational skills 3-5 years of professional experience in student activities, leadership development and/or campus programming. Student affairs experience with an emphasis on student development strongly preferred 3 or more years of advising students on personal and academic matters CHARACTERISTICS PREFERRED: Ability to adjust quickly to changing needs on a daily basis. Ability to apply strong problem solving and conflict resolution skills Maintain productive and effective, inclusive working relationships amongst diverse populations including staff, faculty, administration, students, and other internal and external constituents PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Ability to manage multiple projects and competing priorities simultaneously Ability to train and evaluate performance, taking corrective action as needed WORKING CONDITIONS AND PHYSICAL REQUIREMENTS: Sedentary work: Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or negligible amount of force frequently to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects. Sedentary work involved sitting most of the time and occasionally walking and standing. Climbing, walking, crouching, repetitive motions, and ability to communicate appropriately with students/colleagues. Occasional hours outside the normal College work day to attend events, specifically nights and weekends. ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Provide strategic leadership for student engagement, leadership development, student organizations, and co-curricular programs. Supervise Student Engagement staff, student employees, and interns. Advises, trains, and provides support for the Student Government Association, including attending events, facilitating executive board meetings, supporting event coordination and advertising, supply purchases, and budget management. Oversee student organizations, club operations, the Greek Programming Council, and advisor training and support. Direct leadership development initiatives, speaker series, the Student Leadership Conference, and leadership credentialing programs. Lead the planning and assessment of major campus programs, including Orientation, Welcome Week, Family Weekend, community engagement initiatives, and alternative break experiences. Oversee the approval, coordination, and assessment of student events and activities. Manage departmental budgets, student organization funding, and related expenditures. Direct student recognition programs, including annual awards and leadership recognition initiatives. Oversee departmental marketing, communications, website content, and engagement outreach efforts. Maintain accurate records, assessment data, and reports related to student involvement and program effectiveness. Foster collaborative partnerships with campus and community stakeholders to advance student success and engagement. Serve on institutional committees and perform other duties as assigned by the Vice President for Student Affairs."
    },
    "https://fa-ewbi-saasfaprod1.fa.ocs.oraclecloud.com/hcmUI/CandidateExperience/en/sites/CX_1/job/842": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Category: Enrollment Management - Financial Aid JobSchedule: Full time PrimaryLocation: Saint Augustine, FL, United States The Financial Aid Counselor assist with the administration of financial aid, reviews and awards Flagler College named scholarships and second reads awards. Complete various reports to Federal and State reporting guidelines. The Financial Aid Counselor assist with the administration of financial aid, reviews and awards Flagler College named scholarships and second reads awards. Complete various reports to Federal and State reporting guidelines. Additional Responsibilities: Perform duties \\ tasks as prescribed by the Director and Associate Director of Financial Aid Required Qualifications: Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent required (An acceptable equivalent is an AA degree plus a minimum of 2 years of professional office experience.) Preferred Knowledge and Skills: Effective and professional communication skills both verbally and in writing Possess patience and empathy for students and parents by remaining congenial and respectful under stressful conditions while treating others with dignity and respect Student-focused and collaborative, a cooperative attitude Responsive an accessible by responding promptly with appropriate follow through Analytical skills for the review of documents and student files Computer skills and experience in data entry Proficiency in mathematics Organizational skills and accurate record keeping/data entry Ability to multi-task and work in an environment with frequent interruptions Prior financial aid experience ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: Determines financial aid awards, including federal, state, and institutional financial aid awards in compliance with federal, state, and institutional policy, regulation, and law. Evaluates students’ financial aid documents for completeness and accuracy, ensuring that federal, state, and institutional eligibility and application requirements are met. Performs evaluation of student eligibility in accordance with financial aid renewal requirements and works in conjunction with the Registrar’s Office to review eligibility issues pertaining to grades and hours. Completes the application review and selection of Flagler College named scholarship recipients. Maintain the College’s institutional scholarship application to include adding new scholarships and updating the application to include new selection criteria Serves as the liaison across campus for statistical data and information regarding institutional scholarships and scholarship recipients, including compilation of regular reports to campus stakeholders Conduct a review of student financial aid package awards to ensure accuracy and compliance with federal and state regulations as well as institutional policies Participates in College events to provide information on financial aid matters to the local community including students, prospective students, parents, high school personnel, and other organizations Maintains student financial aid records via both physical file and via enterprise software."
    }
  },
